prompts.run:
Use case: identity-preserve. Create a complete smooth RIGHT-FACING RUN animation sprite sheet from the approved character. Image 1 is the APPROVED design master. Preserve this exact chibi Milo identity: chestnut curls, one large brown eye in true RIGHT-FACING side profile, lavender floppy wizard hat with one yellow star and brown band, teal tunic, cream cuffs, gold round cape clasp, brown belt and boots, short plum cape. BOTH HANDS EMPTY. Same thick charcoal outlines and simple colored cartoon shading. No props, particles, ground shadow, floor, text, labels or grid lines. One full character per cell, consistent head/body/hat size and camera. No changing costumes or facial expression. Production sheet: exactly 4 columns, row-major left-to-right then next row; equal square cells 384x384 pixels. Transparent RGBA background. In EVERY cell, the fixed body root is x=192, virtual grounded foot baseline y=324. Maximum complete figure including hat/cape/hands/boots fits x=48..336, y=48..324; minimum safe padding 48 pixels on all edges. Body stays at same horizontal position in every cell. Don't shift a character to center its silhouette. Preserve natural knee tucking inside the fixed cell; do not bake the world jump arc into the sheet. No visible guides or repeated contact pose as a replacement for real in-betweens. Exactly 12 DISTINCT animation frames arranged 4 columns by 3 rows, canvas 1536x1152. One full run cycle, not twelve nearly identical running illustrations. TWO alternating leg cycles with near and far legs changing which is in front. Near leg has the brighter boot, far leg darker/behind torso. Arms swing opposite their legs. Maintain 2 legs, 2 arms, no duplicates. Essential beats in row-major order:
0 near leg forward contact, far leg back raised;
1 near boot supporting BELOW torso with bent knee, far knee swinging forward;
2 near boot trailing at toe-off, far knee passing in front of hips;
3 flight: far knee leads forward, near leg bent trailing, both soles above baseline;
4 far leg extends toward front landing while near heel rises backward;
5 far boot almost contact forward, near leg far back;
6 far boot forward CONTACT, near leg raised back (opposite frame 0, keep facing right);
7 far boot supporting under torso, near knee swings forward;
8 far boot trailing at toe-off, near knee passes forward;
9 flight with near knee leading and far knee trailing, both feet off baseline;
10 near leg extends forward, far heel rises backward;
11 near boot almost at forward contact, flows into frame 0.
Small intentional torso bob 4-8px only, planted support foot meets y324, flight feet above it. Hat and cape follow subtly with motion, no shape/size drifting. Must show leg crossover and flight, NOT same front foot repeated in all cells. Crop nothing. Keep all 12 complete figures individually separated.

prompts.jump:
Use case: identity-preserve. Create a RIGHT-FACING platformer JUMP phase animation sprite sheet from the approved character. Image 1 is the APPROVED design master. Preserve this exact chibi Milo identity: chestnut curls, one large brown eye in true RIGHT-FACING side profile, lavender floppy wizard hat with one yellow star and brown band, teal tunic, cream cuffs, gold round cape clasp, brown belt and boots, short plum cape. BOTH HANDS EMPTY. Same thick charcoal outlines and simple colored cartoon shading. No props, particles, ground shadow, floor, text, labels or grid lines. One full character per cell, consistent head/body/hat size and camera. No changing costumes or facial expression. Production sheet: exactly 4 columns, row-major left-to-right then next row; equal square cells 384x384 pixels. Transparent RGBA background. In EVERY cell, the fixed body root is x=192, virtual grounded foot baseline y=324. Maximum complete figure including hat/cape/hands/boots fits x=48..336, y=48..324; minimum safe padding 48 pixels on all edges. Body stays at same horizontal position in every cell. Don't shift a character to center its silhouette. Preserve natural knee tucking inside the fixed cell; do not bake the world jump arc into the sheet. No visible guides or repeated contact pose as a replacement for real in-betweens. Exactly 8 DISTINCT sequential poses, 4 columns by 2 rows, canvas 1536x768. Fixed full figure scale matches approved run design; one human boy per cell. The art stays in place, physical world movement applied later by game engine. 8 row-major beats:
0 TAKEOFF: back boot pushing off baseline, front knee raised, chest slightly tilted forward;
1 EARLY RISE: both boots off virtual baseline, leading knee forward and back knee starts folding, empty hands lift slightly;
2 TUCK: both knees bend up compactly below tunic, boots tucked, cape trails down-left;
3 APEX: relaxed tucked knees, body upright, hands spread slightly for balance, cape eases toward left;
4 EARLY FALL: knees begin unfolding, empty arms balance, cape lifts up-left;
5 PRE-LANDING: both lower legs extend downward and slightly forward toward virtual baseline, one boot a little ahead, body prepares contact;
6 LANDING COMPRESSION: boot soles both at baseline, knees visibly compressed and torso lower by 8px, hands low, hat and cape subtly settle;
7 RECOVER TO RUN: front foot planted and back foot lifting, torso recovers, opposite arms ready for running.
Same right profile and head proportions in every cell. Tucking legs shortens lower silhouette but head/root doesn't jump upward inside the cell. Distinct rising/falling silhouettes, no full world parabolic trajectory, no full-size changes. Complete hat and cape inside margins.
